{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The knights in a certain kingdom come in two colors. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726bdcb0779fcb4723bfc790d0f677a9981261a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of them are red, and the rest are blue. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the knights are magical, and the fraction of red knights who are magical is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the fraction of blue knights who are magical. What fraction of red knights are magical?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a398918b5aa24e02aede8ba4aaf44dd8e2018b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{2}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{3}{13}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{7}{27}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{2}{7}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"393\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of knights: then the number of red knights is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/3169b28616c9c477cce6c3a23e83efab3c5c6dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{7}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> and the number of blue knights is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb14bc6b4430a174039ce9c5400251f95f327a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{7}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the fraction of blue knights that are magical - then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b30259d95f64f9aa7c6bd36e1583618a23c8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is the fraction of red knights that are magical. Thus we can write the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d34e97fcd26c3d9e9fe52ccfef5f5c2fba2c05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\cdot \\frac{5}{7}k + 2b \\cdot \\frac{2}{7}k = \\frac{k}{6}\\implies \\frac{5}{7}b + \\frac{4}{7}b = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"310\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9fd2661bfea04e74ae1e4a917bcfad5e36ac39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\frac{9}{7}b = \\frac{1}{6} \\implies b=\\frac{7}{54}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We want to find the fraction of red knights that are magical, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/5291983dc52e9e8f53ebfb2171d959f789c23c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b = \\frac{7}{27} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{7}{27}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"158\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> the fraction of red knights who are magical.\n</p><p>Hence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc5ae8067897f8dfd30d2c67dc3844a727f6dbf2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{2}{7} p + \\left( 1 - \\frac{2}{7} \\right) \\frac{p}{2} . \\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>By solving this equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d07bd033fc3421f8bd159b89a70757797816ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\frac{7}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6e75fb730b8605b3529a741e319ea122795294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{7}{27}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> knights. Then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9caa067b8eb7c5e8319c5c33a104aab8eefed75f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot 42=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> red knights and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c3905b74db1935abb5d9a43579f6f09107cd03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42-12=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> blue knights. \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec2f0d5cd619af2d842b8a4fd13ce919cc41d96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 42=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" /> magical knights. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of red magical knights. \n</p><p>Then we have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faacf546e098fb7b4f33e5986628abdd2e1b0a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{12}=2\\cdot \\frac{7-x}{30}=\\frac{7-x}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" />. Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/57118ed96d43739c86db138753ed1f536f0a9e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=84/27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> back gives us the fraction of red magical knights, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fae0f25f822a326fdc18cbf60ef0ae5b66a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{84}{27}}{12}=\\frac{84}{27}\\cdot \\frac{1}{12}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{7}{27}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"198\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~DairyQueenXD\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to Solution 3, let the total number of knights be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> (We can say this because the fractions we know have denominators of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which have a LCM of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />)\n</p><p>This means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e4c8c22be073393e76863654bd4171b56ae7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2}{7} \\times 42 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" /> red knights meaning there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> blue knights\n</p><p>This also means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4025c037c975e5d92b11a25789938e669abfcb69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{6} \\times 42 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> magical knights. This is important information for our next step.\n</p><p>We are given that the fraction of magical red knights is twice the fraction of magical blue knights. As this problem is dealing with the fraction being twice are large and is asking for the fraction, let's just deal with the variable being a fraction. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9ba2bd66bae47ebdda2382ef31dbb4c241e0db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" /> be the fraction of red magical knights. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb163cd220718ff36784eacb6d4c2c2acff4b7fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p}{2q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> is the fraction of blue magical knights.\n</p><p>We know that total number of magical knights from what we figured out before is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so let's use the fraction we figured and make the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bd8c16e8e09d3edc9d649fff9ecdb0971876c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12 \\times \\dfrac{p}{q}) + (30 \\times \\dfrac{p}{2q})= 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"201\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solving this gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb3869316ac560e541c59b914d9c9193c385935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p}{q}=\\dfrac{7}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"61\" height=\"42\" /> or the fraction of red magical knights.\n</p><p>Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b219da2e311686e0a0b447a21a41d461fa0b62a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{7}{27}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~ Batmanstark\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution is similar to Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the fraction of red knights that are magical. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876fba774d252c254bd1496f6a44b4db630e55cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"16\" height=\"34\" /> is the fraction of blue knights that are magical. We can then create an equation in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac1bfd217c758df0cde9fdfc3abaa66bd95ab379.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\frac{2}{7}x+\\frac{5}{7}(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{1}{6} \\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solving, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a4d518b6003deaabf77d1ab3350fc407489fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{7}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6e75fb730b8605b3529a741e319ea122795294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{7}{27}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~avrilavigne\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p9_RH4s-kBA?t=1274\">https://youtu.be/p9_RH4s-kBA?t=1274</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LJ9mxTNSRUU\">https://youtu.be/LJ9mxTNSRUU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ia0Jbe1h_qY\">https://youtu.be/Ia0Jbe1h_qY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RyN-fKNtd3A?t=1190\">https://youtu.be/RyN-fKNtd3A?t=1190</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" s